<h2 id="spaces-duality-section-comparison" class="tex-section"><span data-tag="0E6D">86.10</span> Comparison with the case of schemes</h2>

<p>
We should add a lot more in this section. 
</p>
<p>
<article class="env-lemma" id="0E6E">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0E6E">Lemma <span data-tag="0E6E">86.10.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of quasi-compact and quasi-separated algebraic spaces over $S$. Assume $X$ and $Y$ are representable and let $f_0 : X_0 \to Y_0$ be a morphism of schemes representing $f$ (awkward but temporary notation). Let $a : D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ Y) \to D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ be the right adjoint of $Rf_*$ from Lemma <a href="/tag/0E55" data-tag="0E55">86.3.1</a>. Let $a_0 : D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_{Y_0}) \to D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_{X_0})$ be the right adjoint of $Rf_*$ from Duality for Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/0A9E" data-tag="0A9E">48.3.1</a>. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_{X_0}) \ar@{=}[rrrrrr]_{\text{Derived Categories of Spaces, Lemma \ref{spaces-perfect-lemma-derived-quasi-coherent-small-etale-site}}} &  &  &  &  &  &  D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ X) \\  D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_{Y_0}) \ar[u]^{a_0} \ar@{=}[rrrrrr]^{\text{Derived Categories of Spaces, Lemma \ref{spaces-perfect-lemma-derived-quasi-coherent-small-etale-site}}} &  &  &  &  &  &  D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ Y) \ar[u]_ a }  \]
</div>
  <p> is commutative. </p>
</article> 
</p>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from uniqueness of adjoints and the compatibilities of Derived Categories of Spaces, Remark <a href="/tag/08GH" data-tag="08GH">75.6.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>
